on and communication are critical. Candidate C has difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric, which is a concern. Candidate B has nasty remarks, pretentious, wrong tone. Candidate D is moody and loner, also concerning. Candidate A is unfriendly, also concerning.\n\nAll have some concerns. Which is strongest overall? Perhaps Candidate D has strong technical competence (problem solving, concentration) and responsibility, but moodiness and loner may affect crew cooperation. Candidate B has stress handling and conscientiousness, but interpersonal issues. Candidate A has leadership and anticipation, but unfriendly and unhealthy. Candidate C has decision speed and attention, but communication issues.\n\nWe might argue that Candidate D's strengths in responsibility, problem solving, and concentration outweigh the moodiness, and that moodiness can be managed, while B's nasty remarks indicate a more severe crew cooperation problem. So we could provisionally recommend Candidate D.\n\nLet's craft a public message: reference Agent 2's note about B lacking crew cooperation and negative remarks. Then state that given B's interpersonal concerns, we are leaning toward D, whose strengths in responsibility and problem solving are crucial, and while D is considered moody and a loner, we have no direct evidence of unsafe behavior, and his responsibility may mitigate. So vote for D.\n\nWe must include explicit facts: D takes responsibility seriously, solves problems extremely well, concentrates very well, responds adequately to unexpected events. Also note D is considered moody and a loner. For B: makes nasty remarks, pretentious, sometimes wrong tone, but handles stress well, conscientious.\n\nNow produce output."}
